https://github.com/cblabs-org/u8g2gl ChangeLog

One entry per MINOR for each component, in the form U8G2 uses: the runtime
(the PlatformIO library, runtime-v* tags) and the cli (the npm package u8g2gl,
cli-v* tags). Each PATCH adds a line saying what it added, in the PR that bumps
it. Each runtime line names the U8G2 release it was built and tested against.
The log starts at runtime 0.11 and CLI 0.15 and is not backfilled; earlier
history is in git. See docs/RELEASING.md.


2026-11-14	cli v0.17.xx	U8G2GL
  * 0.17.0: The designer edits u8g2gl.xml and globals.xml through forms,
    beside the XML. The forms are built from a new declarative vocabulary
    of the two files (every element and attribute, its type, default,
    help and accepted spellings), and tests hold the parsers and the forms
    to it, so every attribute has a control. Each form change is one text
    edit and one undo stop, written where the value is, comments kept; new
    values are written in §5.1's canonical form. Problems show on their
    field, and the Explorer lists each file's sections. In u8g2gl.xml the
    display setup is chosen with a picker (controller, size and variant,
    bus wiring, or search), with a preview of every screen at the new size
    before it is used; bus fields follow the bus family, and a value for
    another family is flagged, not dropped. Targets are added, renamed,
    reordered and removed. The status bar names the active target and
    switches between them: a per-browser view setting, never written to
    the XML. ui_spec §2 gains principle 8, "everything is discoverable",
    and design_spec §5.1 drops the default="true" it never honoured: the
    first target is the default. No change to generated output.
2026-11-10	runtime v0.12.xx	U8G2GL
  * 0.12.0: Implements schema 0.6 (U8G2GL_SCHEMA_VERSION_MINOR 6). Schema
    0.6 adds only an optional icon on <api>, which the designer's Palette
    draws and no generated file carries, so the runtime's behaviour is
    unchanged. Code generated by CLI 0.15 and earlier asserts schema 0.5
    and must be regenerated, because the schema guard compares the minor
    exactly while the major is 0.
    Built and tested against U8G2 2.36.18.
2026-11-10	cli v0.16.xx	U8G2GL
  * 0.16.5: The designer's Explorer lists each screen's elements under it,
    nested as written and in draw order, from the unsaved buffer. A row
    selects its element (opening its screen when another is drawn), and a
    canvas or XML selection lights its row; the tree has the usual keys.
    Each row has an eye that hides the element in the designer only:
    never in the XML, undo, generated code or a test run, which still
    draws the exported view. A hidden element is not drawn, hit or
    outlined; the canvas toolbar shows "N hidden · Show all" and a
    screen's menu offers Show all elements. Rows the sample data hides on
    the device carry a separate mark. The project editor Wasm is rebuilt
    when the CLI's framework sources change. No change to generated
    output.
  * 0.16.4: The designer's property panel puts each property's help in a
    tooltip, as the Palette does for elements, instead of beneath its
    control. An ⓘ after the name opens it on hover, click or keyboard
    focus, as does hovering the name; it shows the help and a facts line with the
    type, an enum's values or a binding's subject types, and the default.
    Escape closes it and leaves the selection alone. Why a field is
    disabled, its problems and the computed-value note stay inline.
    u8g2gl_label's long_mode help is rewritten as user help, and its three
    scroll props now say "Used only when long_mode is scroll or
    scroll_circular." No change to generated output.
  * 0.16.3: The designer's canvas has an Outlines toggle, beside freeze,
    that boxes every drawn element on the overlay, never in the frame, and
    is remembered per browser. A single selected line, hline or vline
    shows a round handle at each end instead of box handles: a line's end
    moves that vertex, and an hline's or vline's end moves along its axis
    with the other end held. A selected line no longer says it cannot
    resize on an axis it has no handle on. No change to generated output.
  * 0.16.2: The designer's first-use fixes. The activity bar draws Lucide
    icons. Saving is visible and stays explicit: the status bar offers
    "● N unsaved · Save", the canvas toolbar has Save for the screen it
    draws, the Explorer marks unsaved files, ⌘S with no editor tab saves
    the canvas's screen and ⌘⌥S saves all. A line's or triangle's handles
    scale its points, and a vertex drags alone; a circle's or ellipse's
    handles change its radii. Circles, ellipses, hlines, vlines and
    pixels can now be selected on the canvas, boxed by what they draw.
    The property panel says why a selected element cannot be resized.
    No change to generated output.
  * 0.16.1: The designer says when its design session ends: a banner
    names the unsaved files and the command for a new session, a failed
    save shows "not saved" in the status bar and brings Output forward,
    and a reload with unsaved changes asks first. A browser opening a
    refused designer link gets a page saying how to start a session,
    instead of JSON; API callers still get JSON. No change to generated
    output.
  * 0.16.0: Schema 0.6: <api icon="..."> names the widget's Palette icon
    from the vendored Lucide set, by name or alias, with a "did you mean"
    for a near miss. The validator accepts 0.4, 0.5 and 0.6; a 0.4 or 0.5
    project using icon is told to declare 0.6. Every framework manifest
    carries its icon, and the Palette reads it from the manifest, falling
    back to the category's icon, then a generic one. Generated code
    requires runtime 0.12.0.
2026-11-03	runtime v0.11.xx	U8G2GL
  * 0.11.1: The runtime version check compares PATCH as well as MINOR:
    U8G2GL_REQUIRE_RUNTIME_AT_LEAST(major, minor, patch), which the
    generator now emits. The two-argument U8G2GL_REQUIRE_RUNTIME_VERSION
    stays, so code generated by CLI 0.15.1 and earlier still compiles.
    The first runtime release tagged under the release scheme.
    Built and tested against U8G2 2.36.18.
2026-11-03	cli v0.15.xx	U8G2GL
  * 0.15.2: Generated code requires runtime 0.11.1 or newer, compared on
    PATCH. The packed CLI reports, and stamps into generated code, its
    release tag's full version (0.15.2-beta.1 on the beta channel). Packing
    needs a cli-v* release tag at HEAD, and a release is published from the
    packed tarball. The first CLI release tagged under the release scheme.
